Subject: [PATCH 10287/11362] Resume the holdout-equalized A/B on the selfparse
 transport, and give the supervisor a rung that reaches it

TRANSPORT WAS UNREACHABLE FROM THE A/B. The arm script pops
CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_TOOL_LOOP before importing the loop, because when it was
written the tool arm had exactly one transport. Setting the variable from outside
would have been silently discarded, so a run believing it measured selfparse
would have measured native tools instead -- the third instance this session of
"verified through a path production never takes". Added --tool-transport
{native,selfparse}, defaulting to native so the 13 banked cells keep meaning what
they meant, and recorded the choice in each shard's meta so a shard can never be
read as the other transport's evidence. The branch is a pure function,
transport_env(), tested off-GPU: 3 mutations RED, including one where the SINGLE
arm also receives the variable, which would quietly turn the control arm into a
second treatment arm and compare a loop against a loop.

RUN STARTED, in its own directory. results/holdout_equalized_ab_selfparse_
20260829, tool arm, GPU 1 (the outer loop's card; the conductor owns GPU 0).
NOT resumed into the 08-20 directory, deliberately: those cells used the native
transport, which the scored vLLM server cannot run at all -- it is launched with
no --enable-auto-tool-choice and returns HTTP 400 on any request carrying tools.
The README records why the two must never be pooled, and one thing the stop note
did not anticipate: the control arm has to be re-run here rather than borrowed,
because the goal-prompt RLE change (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6740) altered prompt
construction after those cells were banked, so pairing across the two dates would
compare across a prompt change as well as across the arm. Cost from the stop
note: tool arm ~598s/cell, single arm ~4,238s/cell, so the tool arm is hours and
the control is days. Tool arm runs first.

SUPERVISOR: A FOURTH RUNG, DEFAULT OFF (REQ-ARC-WMTE-6760). The ladder's second
rung buys a fresh world model but re-draws through the SAME single-shot induction
that just failed to explain the level. tool_loop_reinduction is a different draw:
the model queries transitions and executes candidate engines instead of writing
one blind. It fires only after allow_reinduction has been spent on this level and
stagnation continued -- reaching it with every earlier arm used is exactly the
"all arms exhausted" state the refinement spec calls the written specification
for a new arm.

It is gated OFF behind CARNOT_ARC_SUPERVISOR_TOOL_ARM=1, exact-match, and that
gate is the point. The selfparse gate passed at ceiling on 2026-08-28, so the
loop RUNS; whether it induces BETTER is what the A/B above measures and that has
not reported. Wiring an unmeasured lever into the live scored path is what these
disciplines exist to stop, and leaving the supervisor unable to reach a
capability it should be finetuning against is the opposite failure. A default-off
arm that still appears in arm_outcomes avoids both: its fired/helped counts can
be read before it is trusted, which is the only way it can ever be promoted or
retired on evidence.

Registered as unevaluated in ops/arc_flag_ledger.yaml (via --discover, 131 flags
tracked, 1 new) so it cannot drift into the trusted set silently.

34 supervisor tests, 4/4 mutations RED: arm on by default, any-truthy-value arms
it, fires without re-induction spent, and the gate ignored entirely.

